Only these route-local modules plus report-level claims explicitly marked canonical in `docs/state/theorem-state.yaml` are canonical Target C theorem sources at audit.53. Sections 110--121 are canonical report-level entries and are linked below. The exact train-coupled floor endpoint exclusion is also canonical; its detailed proof and independent audit are linked below. The file `95-protected-contact-creation-obstruction-audit.md` remains proof-only and is intentionally outside the canonical reading order.

## Scope rule

The §57 ZR/ZF theorem is on the nonisolated positive-contact core `V`, not the full source:

\[
\ker\Omega_V=\operatorname{span}\{\mathbf1,P_x|_V,P_y|_V\},
\qquad
\operatorname{rank}R_{C\cup H}[V]=2v-3.
\]

Contact-isolated source points remain in the global configuration. Do not extend the affine-kernel conclusion to their coordinates.

## Current route

Audit.53 retains the audit.52 full-core structural stack and adds six canonical reciprocal/return/depletion theorems.

The global full-core baseline remains
\[
\mu_D\ge\mu_{\rm hull}+\varepsilon_*,
\qquad
R_F\ge(\kappa_{\rm fr}-o(1))D,
\qquad
\sigma_C=0,
\]
with
\[
\mu_{\rm hull}
=
\frac{\pi+\sqrt{\pi/(2\sqrt3)}}2
=
2.046952730226875\ldots.
\]

The new finite train structure is stronger than the audit.52 \((2,2)\)-sparsity statement. Canonical \`C-RECIPROCAL-TRAIN-GRAPH\` integrates positive contact equilibrium into actual reciprocal face coordinates. The bounded-endpoint internal train graph is simple and every nontrivial induced connected component \(U_i\) satisfies
\[
e(U_i)\le2|U_i|-3.
\]
Canonical \`C-OUTER-TRAIN-DETERMINATION\` gives
\[
|\mathcal O|\ge q-k,
\]
where \(\mathcal O\) is the family of old-outer-ended stopped trains.

Canonical \`C-GLOBAL-FACE-RETURN-QUOTAS\` makes exceptional-face defect globally spendable as **independent endpoint/face-label currency**. For every selected face family,
\[
Q_{\mathcal F}\le2|S|-4
\]
for a minimum endpoint-inclusive separator, and all demands
\[
r_f=
\max\left\{
0,
\left\lfloor\frac{m_f-4}{2}\right\rfloor-\ell_f
\right\}
\]
can be realized simultaneously by globally vertex-disjoint actual contact paths to distinct loaded vertices.

Canonical \`C-JOINT-BULK-FACE-SEPARATOR\` couples this with unloaded rhombus bulk:
\[
2\sqrt{\pi a_0(R-5k_I)_+}+Q_{\mathcal F}
\le4k-4,
\qquad a_0=\frac{\sqrt3}{2}.
\]
In a quadratic Type-II unloaded-rhombus bulk this forces
\[
p_D\ge\frac{\pi}{4}D+\frac14Q_{\mathcal F_D}-o(D),
\]
and a selected face-defect cluster in radius \(r\) obeys
\[
Q_{\mathcal F}\le(32+4\pi)r+18.
\]
So a persistent linear exceptional-face tail cannot hide in one submacroscopic cluster, or in sublinearly many clusters with sublinear total radius.

Two asymptotic subbranches are now significantly narrower.

- If \(q/D\to\pi\) and \(u_B=o(D)\), canonical \`C-TERMINAL-PHYSICAL-FRUSTRATION\` gives
  \[
  R_{\mathcal O}=o(D^2),
  \qquad
  \liminf R_{\rm phys}/D\ge\kappa_{\rm phys}>0,
  \]
  plus a linear family of pairwise boundary-vertex-disjoint physical direction-frustrated unit walls.
- If \(x_B=b-q=o(D)\), canonical \`C-LOADED-FLAT-PENTAGON-DEPLETION\` produces
  \[
  g_D\ge q-e_{BI}-6(Q-f)-o(D)
  \]
  distinct second-depletable near-flat physical pentagons and forces
  \[
  \boxed{
  e_{BI}+6(Q-f)
  \ge
  sD+2k+\frac{S_U}{2}-o(D),
  \qquad
  s=\sqrt{\pi/(2\sqrt3)}.
  }
  \]

These return paths and walls are not yet path-length currency, spare packing capacity, or an active-diameter motion. The live source-level target remains to combine the smooth exact contact manifold, positive reciprocal train graph, global loaded-return capacity, and forced physical residual into a motion/replacement that respects **all** lower constraints and strictly lowers the maximum active diameter, or forces an exact unit equilateral triangle.

The separate macroscopic-container branch remains open.

